; sqrt(x*x+1) - x cancels for large positive x, and its interval straddles zero,
; so the relative bound is infinite and the conjugate rule cannot fire: the
; divisor sqrt(x*x+1) + x is not provably nonzero on the whole box.  The
; subtraction's condition number is unbounded, so it gets a guarded node.
; SameSign(sqrt(x*x+1), x) rewrites to x > 0 because the root is positive, and
; in that context the divisor is [1, 20.05], which fires the conjugate.
(FPCore (x)
  :name "sqrt(x*x+1) - x"
  :pre (<= -10 x 10)
  (- (sqrt (+ (* x x) 1)) x))
